8.latex:
\textbf{Structural Recursion: Traversal} \\
Breadth First visits a level at a time: \\
\begin{itemize}
    \item 36, 10, 78, 3, 21, 55, 105, ...
    \item Check the current node,
    add children to a queue
\end{itemize} \\
Depth First traverses down a branch: \\
\begin{itemize}
    \item 36, 10, 3, 1, 6, 21, 15, 28, ...
    \item Check current node,
    then left, then right (other orders are possible)
\end{itemize} \\
\begin{tikzpicture}[level distance=1.5cm,
every node/.style={draw, rectangle, minimum size=1em, fill=blue!50}]
\node {36}
child {node {10}
child {node {3}
child {node {1}}
child {node {6}}}
child {node {21}
child {node {15}}
child {node {28}}}}
child {node {78}
child {node {55}
child {node {45}}
child {node {66}}}
child {node {105}
child {node {91}}
child {node {120}}}}};
\end{tikzpicture} \\
Note: a depth first traversal is like the call order of \\
our Fibonacci example.

14.latex:
