19.latex:
\textbf{Mazes – A first problem} \\
For our maze \\
\begin{itemize}
    \item Start at (0,0), Search for (2,3)
    \item Move by expanding the state L,R,U,D as possible
    \item The smaller we make the tree – the faster we find a solution
    \item Identify redundant states
    \item Don't explore redundant states (don't get into loops)
\end{itemize}
This removes whole branches of our tree that are less useful: \\
\begin{itemize}
    \item (0,0), (1,0), (0,0)
    \item (0,0), (1,0), (1,1), (1,0)
    \item (0,0), (1,0), (1,1), (1,0), (0,0)
    \item Etc.
\end{itemize}
Traverse the tree to find the solution: \\
Note, a Depth first search without removing redundant states would explore \\
LRLRLRLR…
