$w^Tx = w_1x_1 + w_2x_2$

\textbf{How can we modify the output?}

\textbf{Let's use the sign of $w^Tx$ to predict the label}

$\text{sign}(w^Tx) = \begin{cases}
+1 & \text{if } w^Tx > 0 \\
-1 & \text{if } w^Tx \le 0
\end{cases}$

\textbf{Why is this visually a line?}

25.latex:
\textbf{Following the recipe: loss function}

\textbf{Step 2: define loss function $L(y, y')$}

\textbf{What does it mean that we have an error?}

\begin{itemize}
    \item True label $+1$, predicted $-1$:
    $y = 1$, $y' = \text{sign}(w^Tx) = -1$
    \item True label $-1$, predicted $+1$:
    $y = -1$, $y' = \text{sign}(w^Tx) = +1$
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Concisely represented as 0-1 loss:}

$L(y, y') = 1[y \neq y']$

\textbf{Or more explicitly as:}

$l_{01}(z) = 1[z \le 0]$ where $z = y(w^Tx)$

27.latex:
\textbf{What we can do...}

\textbf{Perceptron loss:}
$l(z) = \max\{0, -z\}$

\textbf{Hinge loss:}
$l(z) = \max\{0, 1 - z\}$

\textbf{Logistic loss:}
$l(z) = \log(1 + e^{-z})$

\textbf{Reminder:}
$z = y(w^Tx)$

28.latex:
\textbf{Empirical risk minimizer}

\textbf{Step 3: minimize the loss:}

$w^* = \arg \min_{w \in \mathbb{R}^d} \sum_{i=1}^N l(y_i, w^T x_i)$

\textbf{How?}

Follow the gradient direction!

30.latex:
\textbf{The Perceptron Algorithm}

\textbf{Repeat:}

Pick a data point $x_n$ uniformly at random

\textbf{If} $\text{sign}(w^T x_n) \neq y_n$ \textbf{then}

$w \leftarrow w + y_n x_n$

\textbf{If} the data is linearly separable, this algorithm will find the separating hyperplane!

31.latex:
\textbf{How about logistic loss?}

Find the minimizer of
$F(w) = \sum_{i=1}^N l_{logistic}(y_i w^T x_i) = \sum_{i=1}^N \log(1 + e^{-y_i w^T x_i})$

It is actually called logistic regression

\begin{itemize}
    \item Why logistic loss?
    \item Why regression?
\end{itemize}

33.latex:
\textbf{Perceptron vs. logistic regression}

\textbf{Perceptron}
\textbf{Repeat:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Pick a data point $x_n$, uniformly at random
    \item If $\text{sign}(w^T x_n) \neq y_n$ then
    \item $w \leftarrow w + y_n x_n$
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Logistic Regression}
\textbf{Repeat:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Pick a data point $x_n$, uniformly at random
    \item Update $w$ according to
    \item $w \leftarrow w + \sigma(-y_n w^T x_n) y_n x_n$
\end{itemize}

