18.latex:
\textbf{Conversion to CNF}

$B \leftrightarrow (P \vee Q)$

Eliminate $\leftrightarrow$, replacing $\alpha \leftrightarrow \beta$ with $(\alpha \Rightarrow \beta) \wedge (\beta \Rightarrow \alpha)$

\begin{itemize}
    \item $(B \Rightarrow (P \vee Q)) \wedge ((P \vee Q) \Rightarrow B)$
\end{itemize}

Eliminate $\Rightarrow$, replacing $\alpha \Rightarrow \beta$ with $\neg\alpha \vee \beta$.

\begin{itemize}
    \item $(\neg B \vee P \vee Q) \wedge (\neg(P \vee Q) \vee B)$
\end{itemize}

Move $\neg$ inwards using de Morgan's rules and double-negation:

\begin{itemize}
    \item $(\neg B \vee P \vee Q) \wedge ((\neg P \wedge \neg Q) \vee B)$
\end{itemize}

Apply distributivity law ($\wedge$ over $\vee$) and flatten:

\begin{itemize}
    \item $(\neg B \vee P \vee Q) \wedge (\neg P \vee B) \wedge (\neg Q \vee B)$
\end{itemize}

