4.latex:
\textbf{What is Clustering?} \\
Clustering: the process of grouping a set of objects into classes of similar objects \\
\begin{itemize}
\item Objects within a cluster should be similar
\item Objects from different clusters should be dissimilar
\end{itemize}
Clustering is the most common form of unsupervised learning \\
\begin{itemize}
\item Learning from unlabeled raw data
\item A frequent and important task that finds many applications in data science
\end{itemize}

15.latex:
\textbf{Clustering terminology}

\textbf{Hierarchical clustering}
\begin{itemize}
    \item clusters form a hierarchy
    \item computed bottom-up or top-down fashion
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Flat clustering}
\begin{itemize}
    \item no inter-cluster structure
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Hard clustering}
\begin{itemize}
    \item items are assigned to a single unique cluster
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Soft clustering}
\begin{itemize}
    \item items are assigned to one or more clusters
    \item membership often expressed as a real-valued function
\end{itemize}

Kmeans is flat, hard clustering approach

